  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Monday) \nIssued at 1223 PM MST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nMore quiet weather on tap for Thursday. Temperatures will be a \nlittle cooler, and winds behind the aforementioned backdoor front\nwill be slow to wane Thursday morning, but light winds are\nexpected in the afternoon. \n\nUncertainty in the forecast creeps back in starting Friday and\ncontinuing through the weekend. Models suggest a very positively \ntilted upper trough, or weakly closed low, will slide \nsoutheastward across NM, but the specifics on strength and \nplacement are uncertain. And, the GFS/GEFS suggest some energy \nwill retrograde as a low back to the Pacific. Attm, any solution \ndoesn't bring much precipitation to NM Friday through the \nweekend, so a quiet forecast is maintained, with PoPs<20%, \ntemperatures at or below normal, light winds and passing high \nclouds. Models diverge significantly more starting Monday given \nthe uncertainty in the low placement.",
